ed the Italian economy  and in parallel you started calling for  change in the European Union economic  governance  you have always stressed The crucial  link between Investments on one hand and  reforms on the other hand and to put it  in your words  public Investments are the fuel of  economic growth  but reforms are the engine  and this philosophy has been our Guiding  Light throughout these years of pandemic  and War  today I would like to mention three  examples  on how the right mix of Investments and  reforms  is moving Europe forward  let me begin with Next Generation EU  Next Generation EU our 800 billion euros  plan to boost and modernize Europe's  economy after the pandemic  the Next Generation EU and Italy is a  perfect match  Italy is receiving more than 190 billion  euros for Investments and reforms  almost 67 billion euros have already  been handed over to Italy  and their impact is starting to be very  visible  I know for example  that bocconi and the three other  universities in Milan  have just launched a project  called Musa  for urban regeneration  funded by Next Generation EU  you are mobilizing 700 researchers and  joining forces  with 20 private companies from the  energy sector  to the pharmaceutical sector and to the  chips industry  and together you will Design  the city of the future  powered by Clean Energy  and with clean transport for all  that will host high-tech companies and  create new well-paying jobs  so I am very proud that Europe is  investing in such an ambitious and good  project  besides unprecedented Investments  Next Generation you has also promoted  some crucial reforms  one of them is the reform of public  administration  and I know that some professors from  bocconi have been closely involved in  this in the its Inception thank you very  much for that  but also reforms to reduce for example  late payments  or bureaucracy for small companies  or reforms to accelerate procedures for  renewable energy and I'll come back to  that later  as you say Mario reforms are the engine  of Italy's economy  they can really boost the recovery  my second point  is on investment and reforms  to make energy more affordable  Italy is one of the countries that was  hit the hardest  by Russia's gas blackmail  Putin has cut its export of pipeline gov  to Europe  by 80 percent in only eight months  but we have managed to compensate  and to diversify  and Italy makes a perfect example  you used to import 40 of your gas from  Russia  and now that share is down to roughly 10  percent  thanks to an impressive effort to  diversify your supply  Europe storages  were filled by 96 percent at the  beginning of November  so with all these measures we're safe  for this winter  but of course this comes at a tough  price and that is the price of energy  and therefore in parallel  we have worked on a set of measures to  bring down the prices  we have  insisted  on a solidarity contribution  on the extra profits of energy companies  it will generate roughly 4 billion euros  in revenues here in Italy already in  2023  it is money to support vulnerable  households and vulnerable businesses  we are also working on a joint purchase  of gas because if we go to the markets  to buy gas it is much better we go as 27  we have much more Market power than by  going individual and driving up the  prices like that so we can get better  prices with joint purchase  and we have proposed the so-called  Market correction mechanism which is  basically a price cap  Italy has demanded it from the very  beginning thank you Italy for that  it will prevent  excessive spice hikes  price hikes it will cut manipulation  and what will cut speculation  and as we speak right now member states  are discussing on how to make it fit for  all of the European Union I'm very  confident will have it in place before  the end of the year  but now  we must focus on the next winter  not this one he was safe for this winter  but the next year and the next winter  there is still a gap to be filled  but the good news is the reassuring news  in a very difficult story is that we  have the potential but it is just  untapped  and this potential is renewable energy  this year we have achieved the largest  growth in renewable energy in the  history of the European Union  50 additional gigawatts  which is double of what we had added  last year  and we could accelerate even more it's  not figures from the European commission  but the International Energy agency that  tells us  that we could replace another 14 billion  cubic meter of Russian gas already next  year  if we are speeding up the renewable  projects the renewable energy these  projects are ready to go  but they are stuck because of slow  permitting so we have therefore just  passed a new emergency regulation to  immediately unblock renewable energy  projects now  because ladies and gentlemen my dear  friend renewable energy is not only good  for the climate climate and for the  planet yes it is good for that  but renewable energies are also good for  our independence because they are  homegrown  and they are affordable compared to  fossil fuel fossil fuels are much more  expensive than renewable energy so let's  go for the clean and independent version  of energy and this is renewable energy  I think we should work now together on  the necessary reforms to accelerate the  green transition  Italian families do need clean and  affordable energy  and Italian industry also need clean and  affordable energy  and therefore let's have a look at the  business sector  Italy is home to some of the most  Innovative companies small and  medium-sized  so the industrial basis is strong  but the cost of energy  is heavily Weighing on them  and the only sustainable way out as  we've just discussed discussed is the  transition to renewable energy that is  not only affordable but homegrown but  this transition from fossil fuels to  renewable energy takes time  and the global competition is getting  tougher  as you know  the United States has just presented a  massive investment plan  into the clean tech sectors  the so-called inflation reduction Act  I must say first of all it is good that  the United States is joining us in  decarbonizing their economy that's good  it matters  because the United States is the second  largest emitter in the world  but  the inflation reduction act can also  create distortions  by for example privileging U.S firms  it is the buy American logic that  underpins part of the IRA  it is tax breaks that could lead to  discrimination and it is production  subsidies that could discriminate  European companies  so we have to address this  and this is why we are thinking about  three different lines how to nurture our  clean tech industry  the first point is against the backdrop  I just described that we have to adjust  our own state aid rules  we have to make it simpler for public  investment to power the transition  our stated rules exist for a very good  reason and you would know it better than  you dear Mario you have been  commissioner for competition  so you know it that it is necessary that  they have to make sure that companies  from all member states can compete on  equal footing inside the single Market  however now we have to take a fresh look  this includes for example how we can  make our state aid Frameworks more  predictable  and more simple and faster  or how we can support the whole value  chain  down to the mass production of the most  strategic green text Solutions  and clean end products  so lots of strategic work to do  but  we also know that not all member states  have the same capacity to invest in  their budgets in strategic sectors and  this is my second point  not all member states have the fiscal  space for state aid so we need  complementary European financing to  Foster this clean tech across the whole  European Union  and this is where repower EU comes into  play  repower you is our new plan to overcome  our energy dependency on Russia  repower EU would mean 9 billion euros in  clean energy Investments for Italy  I have now proposed to further boost we  power EU to accelerate the clean  transition all across the European Union  that's a short term  in the midterm  we need a structural solution for our  clean tech industry  the goal of our European policy is  for European industry to be leaders  world leaders in the clean transition  so this is why I introduced the idea of  establishing a sovereignty fund  the logic behind it is very simple  if we have a common European industrial  policy  this requires a common European funding  so here too  this is about strategic decisions  that would allow us to maintain Global  Leadership  and my third point is that we are very  closely working with the Biden  Administration right now on the most  concerning aspects of the IRA  and this concludes for example that we  have joined efforts  on several clean tech sectors  where we Face together the same  challenges  we face for example the challenge  together  that we are developing an over  dependency on China  if it is about raw materials that are  critical for our green transition  so one of the possible solutions could  be to create  a raw materials Club  to overcome China's Monopoly in this  field  we have a lot of good work ahead of us  but important is the message  that one thing is for sure  the US and the European Union  We Stand stronger  individually  When We Stand Together collectively  ladies and gentlemen  my final Point has to do with the reform  of our economic governance  you have worked so much on this Mario  so I'm glad that we have delivered a new  proposal  which I think resonates with everything  dear Mario  that you have been saying for almost 10  years now  we have listened very carefully  you've always said that the future of  our children  needs both  that we invest in sustainability  but also that we invest sustainably  and this is why we want to give National  governments more flexibility on their  debt reduction path  to open the space for strategic  Investments  the Mastery targets do not change  what changes is how we get there  there will be a common European  framework  in which member states will design a  plan  on how to achieve a gradual reduction of  public debt  where Investments and reforms will go  hand in hand  there will be more freedom to invest  but also more scrutiny on the process  once the plan has been agreed and thus  tougher implementation  with this proposal  we could move past a Whole Decade  of divisive debates on our economic  governance in the European Union  it is an economic government that  governance that works for Europe  because it works for all member states  and I believe  dear Mario  that this is also what you have always  strived for throughout your entire  career  roughly one year ago you said  Europe is trying to find a new balance  between sustainability  reforms  and investment to support demand end of  quote  and I'm so grateful for your  contribution dear Mario to finding this  balance  I know that you will leave as your  legacy a new Research Center on European  policy right here at bocconi and I'm  sure  it will become an important resource in  our work at the commission  and I will still count  on your advice my dear friend in the  years to come we're speaking on a  regular basis  I have the questions you have the  precious advice for me  Europe needs your wisdom  Europe needs your capacity  to build Bridges  to build Bridges between Academia  and politics  as always between the North and the  South  but also reaches between the  difficulties of the present  and the brighter future for all  so ladies and Gentlemen please join me  in congratulating a great Italian  a great Economist and a great European  grazia  [Applause]  [Music]

